413 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 187 0 R
/E (Do you have specific projects or positions to offer at the moment?  We do! We are actively recruiting a PhD student to work on the mineralogy and geochemistry of rare earth elements \(REEs\) in sedimentary deposits along the Atlantic Seaboard. Research will focus on rapid-throughput characterization of a large surface and stratigraphic sample set - working across a wide range of analytical methods to generate records of major/trace elements in bulk samples and isotopic variability in individual mineral grains. The student will have 36 months of support through a recent US DoE CORE-CM grant: CM-MAP Critical Minerals in Atlantic Seaboard Plain and the opportunity to collaborate broadly across a range of academic, industry and agency partners. Read more about the broader scope of the project here: https://www.energy.gov/cmei/articles/does-office-critical-minerals-and-energy-innovation-launches-regional-consortia and here: https://sciences.gatech.edu/news/mining-new-possibilities-critical-minerals-mapping-stronger-us-supply-chain. The student would be based in the Georgia Tech School of Earth and Atmospheric Sciences in Atlanta, Georgia. You can read more about the EAS PhD program here: https://eas.gatech.edu/prospective-graduate-students the application deadline is January 1, 2027. Interested students should contact Dr. Karl Lang \(karl.lang@eas.gatech.edu\) and Dr. Isaiah Bolden \(iwb@gatech.edu\) via email for additional information. Otherwise, undergraduate students interested in research experiences with us are more than welcome to apply for our department's NSF REU Program: https://easreu.eas.gatech.edu/)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [8 594 0 R 10 595 0 R 12 596 0 R]
>>
